nfig, push to Git.\\\\\\\\n   1. Scaffold RootLayout.tsx with NavBar + Footer placeholders.\\\\\\\\n   2. Implement Tailwind config (color palette, typography, dark mode).\\\\\\\\n   3. Implement NavBar component with mobile Disclosure, active link styles.\\\\\\\\n   4. Create ProtectedRoute.tsx HOC using useAuth(); unit-test.\\\\\\\\n   5. Generate static pages: Home, Schools, Bylaws (fetch from CMS).  [OFAAT per page]\\\\\\\\n   6. Build Contact page with react-hook-form & API route /api/contact.\\\\\\\\n   7. Build DuesDashboard page behind ProtectedRoute, placeholder data.\\\\\\\\n   8. Build AnnualMeetings page likewise.\\\\\\\\n   9. Build NewsEventsList & Detail pages with ISR fetch.\\\\\\\\n   10. Build AdminShell (layout only) behind AdminRoute; expose CRUD components stub (to be filled by CMS team).\\\\\\\\n   11. Implement Footer with dynamic year & ADA link.\\\\\\\\n   12. Add jest-axe & run baseline a11y tests for each page.\\\\\\\\n   13. Manual cross-browser QA (Chrome, Safari, Edge) desktop + mobile.\\\\\\\\n   14. Lighthouse run; fix contrast/performance issues.\\\\\\\\n   15. Prepare Storybook for UI components (optional, low priority).\\\\\\\\n   16. Demo to stakeholders; iterate.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n10. Subordinate Recruit Needs (Supervisor Rank)\\\\\\\\n   S-1  “Frontend Architecture Supervisor”      – set up Next/Tailwind, repo tooling.\\\\\\\\n   S-2  “Routing & Guard Supervisor”            – implement ProtectedRoute/AdminRoute + unit tests.\\\\\\\\n   S-3  “Page Delivery Supervisor”              – oversee content pages (Home, Contact, Schools, Bylaws).\\\\\\\\n   S-4  “Protected Dashboards Supervisor”       – build Dues & Annual Meetings pages.\\\\\\\\n   S-5  “Admin/CMS UI Supervisor”               – build News & Events CRUD/admin screens & CMS hooks.\\\\\\\\n   S-6  “A11y & QA Supervisor”                  – enforce WCAG, jest-axe, Lighthouse, cross-browser tests.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nNo immediate RECRUIT calls issued until DEP approval.\\\\\\\\n\\