\\n    match /boardData/{docId} { allow read, write: if request.auth.token.role in ['board','superadmin']; }\\\\\\\\n    match /{document=**} { allow read, write: if request.auth!=null; }\\\\\\\\n  }\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. Cloud Storage Rules\\\\\\\\nservice firebase.storage {\\\\\\\\n  match /b/{bucket}/o {\\\\\\\\n    match /user_uploads/{uid}/{all=**} { allow read, write: if request.auth.uid==uid; }\\\\\\\\n    match /board_assets/{file=**} { allow read, write: if request.auth.token.role in ['board','superadmin']; }\\\\\\\\n  }\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n5. Next.js Integration Strategy\\\\\\\\n   • Packages: firebase, firebase-admin, cookie, js-cookie, jsonwebtoken.\\\\\\\\n   • Client: firebaseClient.ts, AuthContext.tsx exposing {user, loading, role}.\\\\\\\\n   • HOC/Hook: withAuth(Component, requiredRole?), useAuth().\\\\\\\\n   • Server: firebaseAdmin.ts (singleton), middleware.ts verifies token cookie, sets x-user-role header, redirects unauth.\\\\\\\\n   • API helper getAuthUser(req) verifies cookie via admin SDK.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n6. Auth Token Flow\\\\\\\\n   After login: user.getIdToken() → httpOnly Secure cookie “token” (SameSite=Lax, 1h). Refresh listener renews. Logout clears.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n7. Dev / CI / Deploy\\\\\\\\n   • .env.local & Vercel env vars for client + admin.\\\\\\\\n   • GitHub Actions inject secrets.\\\\\\\\n   • firebase emulators:run + Jest unit tests.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n8. Dependency Handoffs\\\\\\\\n   A) CMS team → board claim access, useAuth() hook.\\\\\\\\n   B) Front-End → withAuth HOC, AuthContext, file-upload helper paths.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n9. Validation & Testing\\\\\\\\n   • Unit tests on rules via @firebase/rules-unit-testing.\\\\\\\\n   • Cypress e2e: auth, cookie, redirects, board access.\\\\\\\\n   • Security scan (npm audit, Snyk).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n10. Roll-out / Migration\\\\\\\\n   1) Merge PR behind feature flag → staging QA.\\\\\\\\n   2) Promote to prod → seed superadmin.\\\\\\\\n   3) Onboard board users via