      contentHtml         STRING                // generated server-side for display\\\\\\\\n      coverImageURL       STRING (Storage path)\\\\\\\\n      tags                ARRAY<STRING>\\\\\\\\n      status              STRING  {draft,published}\\\\\\\\n      authorUid           STRING\\\\\\\\n      createdAt           TIMESTAMP (server)\\\\\\\\n      updatedAt           TIMESTAMP (server)\\\\\\\\n      publishedAt         TIMESTAMP|null\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n   B) Collection  minutes\\\\\\\\n      id (docId)\\\\\\\\n      meetingDate         TIMESTAMP\\\\\\\\n      title               STRING\\\\\\\\n      summary             STRING (short)\\\\\\\\n      fileURL             STRING  (/minutes/{id}.pdf)\\\\\\\\n      access              STRING {public,boardOnly}\\\\\\\\n      uploaderUid         STRING\\\\\\\\n      createdAt,updatedAt TIMESTAMP\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n   C) Collection  dues\\\\\\\\n      id\\\\\\\\n      residentUid         STRING\\\\\\\\n      amount              NUMBER (cents)\\\\\\\\n      periodStart         TIMESTAMP\\\\\\\\n      periodEnd           TIMESTAMP\\\\\\\\n      status              STRING {paid,unpaid,past-due}\\\\\\\\n      receiptURL          STRING (optional Storage path)\\\\\\\\n      processedByUid      STRING|null\\\\\\\\n      createdAt,updatedAt TIMESTAMP\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3.  Firebase Auth & Role-Based Access\\\\\\\\n   • Onboard users normally with Firebase Auth (email+password or OAuth).\\\\\\\\n   • Assign custom claims  {role:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"board\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}  via Admin SDK CLI or Cloud Function.\\\\\\\\n   • Middleware (Next.js) validates ID token ⇒ redirects unauth/unauthorized.\\\\\\\\n   • Firestore & Storage rules reference request.auth.token.role.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4.  Security Rules (deterministic snippets)\\\\\\\\n   Firestore example:\\\\\\\\n   service cloud.firestore {\\\\\\\\n     match /databases/{db}/documents {\\\\\\\\n       match /posts/{doc} {\\\\\\\\n         allow read: if true;                                   // public\\\\\\\\n         allow write: if request.auth.token.role == 'board';\\\\\\\\n       }\\\\\\\\n       match /minutes/{doc} {\\\\\\\\n         allow read: if resource.data.access == 'public' ||\\\\\\\\n                      (request.auth.token.role == 'board');\\\\\\\\n         allow write: if request.auth.token.role == 'board';\\\\\\\\n       }\\\\\\\\n       match /dues/{doc} {\\\\\\\\n         allow read,write: if request.auth.token.role == 'board';\\\\\\\\n       }\\\\\\\\n     }\\\\\\\\n   }\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n   Storage example paths & rules:\\\\\\\\n   • /minutes/** – board write, public/board read based on Firestore doc.access.\\\\\\\\n   • /post_images/** – board write, public read.\\\\\\\\n   • /dues_receipts/** – board read/write.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n5.  Next.js Folder/Route Layout (App Router)\\\\\\\\n   /app\\\\\\\\n     |_ (public) news/page.tsx             – list posts\\\\\\\\n     |_ (public) news/[slug]/page.tsx      – full post\\\\\\\\n     |_ (public) minutes/page.tsx          – list minutes (filtered by access)\\\\\\\\n     |_ admin/\\\\\\\\n          |_ layout.tsx + middleware.ts    – auth wrapper\\\\\\\\n          |_ dashboard/page.tsx            – landing metrics\\\\\\\\n          |_ posts/\\\\\\\\n               |_ page.tsx                 – posts table\\\\\\\\n               |_ new/page.tsx             – create\\\\\\\\n               |_ [id]/page.tsx            – edit\\\\\\\\n          |_ minutes/ (same pattern)\\\\\\\\n          |_ dues/    (same pattern)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n   Shared libs:\\\\\\\\n   • lib/firebase/client.ts  (initializeApp)\\\\\\\\n   • lib/firebase/admin.ts   (admin SDK)\\\\\\\\n   • lib/auth/withRole.ts    (server helper)\\\\\\\\n   • lib/storage/upload.ts   (helper with resumable upload & progress)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n6.  Implementation Steps (Execution Phase)\\\\\\\\n   1. Bootstrap Next.js project, add env vars and Firebase SDKs.\\\\\\\\n   2. Configure firebase project + service account JSON locally.\\\\\\\\n   3. Implement Auth provider & role guard middleware (/admin/*).\\\\\\\\n   4. Build Firestore wrapper functions for each collection (CRUD in /src/services/*).\\\\\\\\n   5. Implement Storage uploader util with path strategy switch (minutes, post_images, dues_receipts).\\\\\\\\n   6. Posts module:  list → table w/ edit+delete; form with Tiptap; image upload integrated.\\\\\\\\n   7. Minutes module:  list; form with PDF upload; ‘access’ selector.\\\\\\\\n   8. Dues module:     table; CSV import helper (optional); receipt upload.\\\\\\\\n   9. Generate public-side pages using incremental static regeneration (ISR) where appropriate.\\\\\\\\n   10. Write Unit tests (Jest + @testing-library/react) for services & components.\\\\\\\\n   11. Finalize Firestore indexes (composite for minutes by date, posts by status+publishedAt, dues by residentUid+periodEnd).\\\\\\\\n   12. Deploy to Vercel (or Firebase Hosting) with CI token secrets.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n7.  Deliverables / Definition of Done\\\\\\\\n   • Admin dashboard reachable at /admin guarded by auth/role.\\\\\\\\n   • Fully functional CRUD for posts, minutes, dues with file uploads.\\\\\\\\n   • Public pages rendering data correctly with SSR/ISR.\\\\\\\\n   • Security rules passing emulator tests.\\\\\\\\n   • Unit test suite ≥ 80 % coverage on critical libs.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n8.  Sub-Agent Needs (Supervisor-rank recruits)\\\\\\\\n   S-1  CMS-UI-Supervisor        – implements dashboard UI components & forms.\\\\\\\\n   S-2  Auth-Security-Supervisor – sets up Firebase Auth, custom claims, middleware, Firestore/Storage rules + emulator tests.\\\\\\\\n   S-3  Storage-Supervisor       – creates upload utilities & integrates with editor/forms; handles Storage rules.\\\\\\\\n   S-4  DataModel-Supervisor     – formalizes schema, indexes, seed/migration scripts, write-side validation.\\\\\\\\n   S-5  PublicSite-Supervisor    – builds public Next.js pages & ISR strategy.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEach Supervisor will later recruit Attendants 